## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a streaming NLP system that handles multiple languages, domain adaptation, drift monitoring, latency budgets, and privacy considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual NER with adapters
- Drift monitoring and active learning
- Domain gazetteers and retrieval augmentation
- Privacy: data minimization and differential privacy
- Evaluation: streaming metrics, latency budgets, OOD checks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-inference sketch with adapters
async function predict(text, model) {
  const tokens = tokenize(text);
  const enc = model.encode(tokens);
  const logits = await model.predict(enc);
  return decodeEntities(logits, tokens);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify and react to drift in production?
- How would you structure the entity schema with provenance and versioning?
- How would you audit and mitigate bias across languages?

## Why This Is Asked

Probes on-device NLP, privacy, and latency trade-offs in edge deployments typical of Cloudflare/Uber-scale products.

## Key Concepts

- On-device inference with deterministic latency
- Regex-based redaction plus tiny ML for edge cases
- Multilingual and code-switching handling
- Privacy controls and local data labeling

## Code Example

```javascript
const redact = (text) => {
  const emails = /[\w.+-]+@[\w.-]+\.[a-zA-Z]{2,}/g;
  const phones = /(\+?\d[\d\s\-\(\)]{7,}\d)/g;
  let out = text.replace(emails, "[REDACTED_EMAIL]");
  out = out.replace(phones, "[REDACTED_PHONE]");
  out = out.replace(/\b[A-Z][a-z]+ [A-Z][a-z]+\b/g, "[REDACTED_NAME]");
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and guarantee 100 ms latency across devices?
- How would you handle false positives and user-triggered corrections without server contact?

## Why This Is Asked

This angle tests end-to-end system thinking across multilingual NLP, streaming latency, privacy-by-design, RAG, and deployment.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual intent classifier with adapters trained on English/Spanish/Japanese corpora
- Streaming ASR integration and latency budgets (target ~150 ms)
- Privacy: data minimization, on-device processing where possible, PII masking, tenant isolation
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation for consistent responses
- Deployment: feature flags, drift monitoring, rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code illustrating a multilingual intent classifier with adapters
const { Tokenizer, Model } = require('transformers-js');
const tokenizer = Tokenizer.fromPretrained('xlm-roberta-base');
const model = Model.fromPretrained('xlm-roberta-base', { numLabels: 50 });
model.addAdapter('multilingual');
model.setActiveAdapters(['multilingual']);
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor model drift across languages and handle changes in intents?
- How would you design a safe fallback path when the classifier has low confidence?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design production-grade, multilingual, real-time NLP with auditability and privacy in a global setting.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming architecture with on-device first-pass
- Retrieval-augmented detection that cites policy clauses
- Privacy-preserving inference (DP/federated) and data provenance
- Drift monitoring, versioned policies, staged rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example integration stub for policy retrieval
async function flagPost(post, policyIndex) {
  const clause = await fetchPolicyClause(policyIndex, post.language);
  const isFlag = await detector.score(post, policyIndex);
  return isFlag ? {postId: post.id, clause} : null;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you evaluate and mitigate false positives across languages during policy updates?
- How do you design the provenance log and audits to satisfy regulatory requirements?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes real-time multilingual NLP design with privacy, per-tenant isolation, and governance. It tests architecture, data flow, error handling, and testing strategies for production-grade latency.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time multilingual inference
- Per-tenant privacy-preserving embeddings
- Unified normalization taxonomy
- Edge-first deployment and latency guarantees
- Drift detection and governance annotation loop

## Code Example
```javascript
// DP-encoder sketch (conceptual)
function dpEncode(text, epsilon) {
  // apply noise to embedding vector
  const vec = embed(text);
  return vec.map(v => v + laplace(0, 1/epsilon));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate drift between tenants without leaking data?
- What rollback strategy would you implement if a taxonomy update causes misclassification?
